<title>USA: Fiat to recall 6,000 Alpha Romeos.</title>
<headline>Fiat to recall 6,000 Alpha Romeos.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-08-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Fiat Auto SpA, a unit of Fiat SpA, said Tuesday it will recall 6,000 1991 to 1993 Alfa Romeo 164 U.S.A. version cars to correct a fuel leak problem.</p>
<p>Fiat said some components of a rubber filler pipe were altered during the manufacturing process that could lead to a decay of the pipe and fuel seepage.</p>
<p>Fiat no longer sells Alpha Romeo cars in the United States.</p>
</text>
